      "id": 455943,
      "username": "jankijoshi",
      "name": "Janki",
      "created_at": "2025-01-31T11:31:14.538Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I have set up a <strong>regular shift</strong> in my system and enabled the <strong>Auto Attendance</strong> option. After selecting Auto Attendance, I filled in all the required shift details, including check-in and check-out times.</p>\n<p>However, despite enabling Auto Attendance, I still have to manually go to the shift settings and click the <strong>Mark Attendance</strong> button every day. I expected the system to automatically mark attendance daily based on the configured check-in and check-out times.</p>\n<h3><a name=\"p-455943-issue-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-455943-issue-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><strong>Issue:</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Auto Attendance is enabled, but it is not marking attendance automatically.</li>\n<li>I still need to manually click “Mark Attendance” every day.</li>\n<li>I want attendance to be marked automatically at a specific time based on check-in and check-out.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><a name=\"p-455943-questions-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-455943-questions-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><strong>Questions:</strong></h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Is there any additional setting I need to enable for full automation?</li>\n<li>Does the system require any background job or scheduler to trigger automatic attendance marking?</li>\n<li>Has anyone faced a similar issue, and how did you resolve it?</li>\n</ol>",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/ecccb3/{size}.png",
